=== SUMMARY ===
data sources : none — the web page owns no hook; it edits in-memory SQL against a static curated catalog. SqlPlaygroundPageViewModel hoists the editor string + Run reduction into StateFlow<SqlPlaygroundUiState>; no HTTP, no shared store. View.opened diagnostic recorded once (surface="SqlPlaygroundPage", P1/S11), carrying no query text.
nav          : Destinations 'powerSql' -> /power/sql (pre-existing metadata row) wired to SqlPlaygroundRoute() via PageHosts.register in TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate; deep link auto-registered by TeslaSyncNavHost.
panels       : GlassPanel1 = Manual SQL editor (PanelTitle + Textarea + Run/Clear + Run help message); GlassPanel2 = Curated schema catalog (PanelTitle + intro + 5 bordered table Cards, by-name sorted, 33 columns total). Both drawn from the StateFlow.
states       : single success state (web manifest declares only "success"). The page is always interactive against the static catalog; there is no remote feed, so there is no loading/empty/error region — nothing is ever blank (ADR-011). The Run help message renders runEmpty (defensive, button disabled while blank) and runUnavailable from state.runOutcome.
ai-drafter   : web <AINLSqlPlayground/> is a separate feature-gated shared-surface unit (NOT in the 14 required items); its AI-gate + SSE source is not exposed by DataContainer and wiring it is outside this prompt's allowed files. Documented above; the manual baseline is implemented in full; not stubbed.
a11y/theme   : MaterialTheme/TeslaTokens tokens only (dark + dynamic, ADR-005/015); non-merging semantics contentDescription on both panels + each table Card; liveRegion=Polite on the Run message (web role="status"); >=48dp Button targets (Material 3).
units        : N/A at the display boundary (no unit-bearing computed value; catalog SI column names are schema text, ADR-013) — never stored/computed non-SI.
